es of winning the national championship this season a long shot.","published":"2026-11-22T04:06:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/49921234/college-football-betting-buzz-odds-updates-line-moves-spreads","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Emotional Greg Schiano authors 'special' win, Rutgers' first at PSU since 1988","description":"Less than two weeks after Rutgers announced embattled Greg Schiano would return as coach for a 19th season, the Scarlet Knights stunned Penn State 25-24 on Saturday, their first win over the Nittany Lions since 1988, and just their third this year.","published":"2026-11-22T02:56:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50557643/rutgers-authors-special-win-1st-penn-state-1988","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4918136/quincy-rhodes-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quincy_Rhodes_Jr."},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Quincy Rhodes Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quincy_Rhodes_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:15Z","intro":"Quincy Rhodes Jr. (born December 1, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Arkansas Razorbacks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Rhodes Jr. attended North Little Rock High School in North Little Rock, Arkansas. As a senior he had 84 tackles and 11.5 sacks. He was selected to play in the 2022 All-American Bowl. Rhodes Jr. committed to the University of Arkansas to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Rhodes Jr. spent his first two years at Arkansas as a backup, appearing in 21 games with one start and recording 16 tackles and one sack. He became a full-time starter for the first time his junior year in 2025."}]}}